            <ArticleTitle>Complete Chloroplast Genome Sequence of Cane Needle Grass, Nassella hyalina (Poaceae: Stipeae).</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01215-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01215-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nassella hyalina (cane needle grass) is on the Alert List for Environmental Weeds in Australia. We present here the first complete chloroplast sequence of N. hyalina reconstructed from Illumina whole-genome sequencing. The complete chloroplast sequence is 137,606 bp in size and has a gene content and structure similar to those of other published chloroplast genomes of Stipeae.</AbstractText>
